We are excited that you've chosen Orlando Health at a place for you and your dog to volunteer. We have an exciting and growing Program. To facilitate your process of becoming a Volunteer, please visit the Orlando Health web site and fill out the online Volunteer Application for the hospital of your choice. Please indicate that you have interest in Pet Therapy in your application. We will then contact you and schedule a time for you and your dog to come in for an interview.  If that all goes well, then you would shadow an existing Pet Therapy team, and then an existing handler would mentor you during your first session with your dog. 

After a successful shadowing and mentoring process you and your dog would be ready to begin volunteering on your own.  Also important to note that only the adult hospitals are currently accepting new pet therapy teams. 

A few important requirements to note - 
The Program requires that all Pet Therapy Volunteers visit the hospital at least two times per month. 
Your dog must be bathed and groomed within 24 hours prior to each visit. 
You must be at least 18 years old. 

